  'iran_configs': 'Iran configs',
  'iran_configs_1_to_8_no_server': '• **Iran configs (1 to 8):** no server, for opening ordinary sites and apps. The first thing to try.\\n• **Cloud panel (BPB / EDG / Nahan):** your own private server on your own Cloudflare account; the most dependable option for every app, but you have to deploy it once.\\n• **Domain fronting:** no server and no cost, but browser-only and it needs a certificate installed.\\n• **Gaming tab:** for lowering game ping, not for opening sites.\\n• **Emergency:** for when everything is blocked and you cannot even fetch a config.',
  'iran_home_footer': 'Built-in configs from the upstream Serverless-for-Iran project, shipped untouched. They reach Cloudflare directly with a fragmented TLS handshake and no server of ours in the path, so there is nothing to deploy and nothing to pay for. Each varies the DNS resolver and how the handshake is chopped, so when one operator blocks a fingerprint another still connects. Anything you add to this folder yourself appears here too.',
  'iran_test_action': 'Test these on your connection',
  'iran_test_footer': 'These configs have no server: they ask a DNS-over-HTTPS resolver for every name. If that resolver cannot be reached on your connection, no name resolves and no site opens — however healthy the rest of the config is. This measures exactly that and, in a few seconds, says which rows stand a chance at all. Which of them actually gets past the filtering only shows once you connect.',
  'iran_test_row_bad': 'Its DNS resolver could not be reached (%1\$s)',
  'iran_test_row_ok': 'Its DNS resolver answered (%1\$d ms) — worth trying',
  'iran_test_running': 'Measuring…',
  'is_always_tested_first_it_also_runs': 'is always tested first. It also runs fewer tests at once so the numbers stay honest.',
  'is_applied_to_the_next_connection_that': 'is applied to the next connection. That is also why nothing appears in the phone\\\'s status ',
