  'it_means_android_has_not_accepted_the': 'It means Android has not accepted the certificate yet. There are three common reasons: 1) at the certificate-type step you did not choose “CA certificate” (choosing VPN or Wi-Fi installs it but is no use to us); 2) you picked the wrong file — it has to be MLM-VPN-Certificate.crt; 3) your phone has no screen lock (PIN, pattern or fingerprint) — Android will not install a certificate until you set one. You do not need to close and reopen the app; it checks constantly and ticks the moment the certificate is installed.',
  'it_means_that_server_s_country_is': 'It means that server\\\'s country is no longer the list\\\'s claim but a measurement. After you actually connect to a server, the app asks Cloudflare from inside that tunnel where the traffic came out. If the answer differs from the old flag, the server is moved to its real country for good and you are told. The reason is that when someone picks a country, the point is to come out in that country.',
